{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>תורת</b> — Rav Saadia the Gaon [Saadia] said: that the word יאמר is missing, for the sun says תורת השם תמימה. And in my opinion: he has mentioned thus far how the discerning person can find testimony to the divinity and know His deeds, and David said that there is also another witness, more honored than it and more trustworthy, and it is the Torah of HaShem and His testimonies and His precepts and His commandments and His fear and His judgments." "And the meaning of תורה — that it teaches the straight way by means of mentioned signs, like תורת הצרעת and תורת הנזיר." "And he mentioned משיבת נפש — because the Torah removes doubt from the soul." "And the reason for saying תמימה — corresponding to the sun, because the sun is perfect in its light and is not like the moon." "And the reason for משיבת נפש — like the sun, for from the time the sun is in the ascending half of the sphere, the soul of many sick returns, the opposite of what happens when it is in the descending half, and the physicians knew this, and the testimony of the ancients transmitted it from those who witnessed it with their own eyes. And because a person cannot know them by way of proofs, he said: מחכימת פתי. And he said that they are trustworthy and not lies, even though the wise of heart do not know them, and he said of the Torah that it is תמימה, for it does not need the testimony of another witness alongside it."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:52.490846219Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}